+# SystemPageFileInformationEx (class 144) as 64-bit Windows returns it, one entry per active page file: NextEntryOffset,
+# TotalSize, TotalInUse, PeakUsage (4 unsigned 32-bit), the name as a UNICODE_STRING (Length, MaximumLength as unsigned
+# 16-bit, 4 bytes of padding, a 64-bit pointer), MinimumSize, MaximumSize (2 unsigned 32-bit): 40 bytes. The sizes are
+# in pages of the system page size. Layout as in System Informer's phnt/include/ntexapi.h
+# (SYSTEM_PAGEFILE_INFORMATION_EX); Microsoft documents that such internal structures can change, so the parser checks
+# every count, offset and name bound against the returned bytes and returns None on anything else.
+PAGEFILE_EX_FORMAT = "<IIIIHH4xQII"
+PAGEFILE_EX_BYTES = struct.calcsize(PAGEFILE_EX_FORMAT)
